On Friday, 6 September 2019 18.56.42 EDT Xabju wrote:
> Hello all,
> 
> Beginner here looking for some help. Wondering if this nonsensical verse
> parses:
> 
> le skaci cakcinki cu sakcti ci cidja
> .i je ca sy. ckaji ci skaci selcitka
> 
> 
> It should read, "The 'skirt-beetle' suckingly eats three foods, and it is
> now characterized by three skirtish eaten-things."

It does parse, but I think you mean ".ije sy. ca ckaji". "ca sy. ckaji" means 
"when it, [missing subject] is characterized".

Pierre

